{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"36082ae0b4281f21370786edc93a7d51602c276975a830a4349021b07bb063bc","packTokens":2968,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":700,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1708,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What may Parking Administrators and Security Guards do in the web app, beyond the functions already described?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Administrators manage employee and parking records, assignments, configuration, and report recipients; guards use only the entrance indicator and existing sticker process.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may receive reports that identify employees and their unused parking, and how are recipients maintained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Parking Administrator maintains a named recipient list; only those recipients receive the report.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which source is authoritative for employee profiles, dedicated-parking assignments, and registered vehicles when an employee signs in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee details and an administrator-maintained parking assignment and vehicle list.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For an employee with multiple registered vehicles, what counts as parking utilization when any one of their plates is detected entering that day?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Count the allocation as used if any vehicle registered to that employee is detected.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What makes an employee without dedicated parking eligible to claim a released space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any active Folio3 employee without a dedicated assignment who has at least one registered vehicle may claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a claim after successfully claiming a space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Claims cannot be cancelled by the user once confirmed.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder's released space has been claimed but the holder's permanently stickered vehicle arrives, how should the system treat the temporary claimant's authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the temporary authorization valid; the stickered vehicle continues through the existing process even if this exceeds configured capacity.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall authenticate only active Folio3 employees using corporate Google Workspace identities, returning an authenticated session on success and rejecting personal Gmail, non-Folio3, and inactive identities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"After successful sign-in, the app shall return a profile with corporate-directory employee details and, where present, administrator-maintained parking assignment, floor, and registered-vehicle records, while preventing non-administrators from viewing another employee’s profile.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall require employees without a registered vehicle to register at least one license plate before parking release or claim operations, and vehicle registration shall support an optional make, model, and color.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Parking Administrators shall be able to create, view, and update employee, parking assignment, and registered-vehicle records, and configure daily release time, per-floor capacity, the work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard role assignments; unauthorized changes shall be rejected without changing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Every employee and administrator page shall be a responsive web page usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with no horizontal page overflow and touch-operable primary controls on narrow screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder shall be able to release today’s reserved parking with one action, recording exactly one release for that holder and date and showing its status as Released.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"On configured working days, a dedicated assignment shall show Reserved by default; a same-day release submitted before the configured daily release time shall become claimable at that time in the Folio3 office time zone, and a release submitted later shall be claimable immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"A dedicated holder shall be able to schedule releases for one or more dates no more than 30 days ahead, with each scheduled release becoming claimable at the daily release time on its selected date; the release calendar shall show selected dates and scheduled status, and dates beyond the 30-day limit shall be rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"A holder shall be able to cancel an unclaimed scheduled release, while cancellation of a claimed release shall be rejected and preserve the claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall show claimable parking availability and the current available-space count to active Folio3 employees who have no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle; ineligible employees shall be denied or rejected without creating a claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"For claims on the same last available release, the app shall accept only the earliest claim, reject the other with a conflict, and return the assigned floor from configured floor capacity; each accepted claim shall record the employee, date, time, and allocation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Employees shall not be able to cancel a confirmed temporary parking claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When a released allocation becomes claimable, the app shall email eligible employees who lack dedicated parking and have a registered vehicle, using the configured fixed template.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Recording the arrival of a permanently stickered vehicle shall leave its existing sticker process unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"For LPR entrance verification, the app shall activate the green indicator and authorize entry only when a detected car has a readable plate matching a valid temporary authorization for the current date; non-car detections shall produce no authorization response or indicator activation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"If the plate is unreadable or the LPR, plate-reading service, connection, or indicator cannot verify authorization, the app shall leave the green indicator inactive and deny entry through the temporary-parking process.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, readable plate or an empty plate field, result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Daily utilization shall use registered-vehicle entry records and count an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day; it shall record unused dedicated parking when a dedicated holder has no entry and unused temporary parking when a confirmed claimant has no entry, including the specified employee, vehicle, and date fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"A Monday-morning weekly reporting job in the Folio3 office time zone shall generate a report containing unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and an overall utilization-percentage field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Weekly report emails shall be sent only to addresses in the named report-recipient list configured by a Parking Administrator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Parking Administrators shall be able to filter on-screen utilization records and export the displayed records as a CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3’s existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Phase 1 utilization functionality shall be limited to monitoring, recording, and reporting, without creating automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The responsive web app shall support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the first-year scale assumed for employee accounts and stored records.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}